# Diagrammo Slate — light
# Generated from dgmo/src/palettes/slate.ts; the same sixteen slots that
# diagrammo.app/slate/ publishes. Do not hand-edit a hex here — change the
# palette in dgmo and take the file from the site.
#
# A light ground cannot reuse the palette's own hues directly: even the light
# spectrum leaves yellow at 2.42:1 against white, and that is the slot most
# colored output lands in. So each hue is walked toward black until it clears
# 4.5:1 for normal and 7:1 for bright, holding its hue and spending only
# lightness. Red, blue and purple already clear it and are exactly as the
# palette drew them.
#
# Bright goes DARKER here while bright black stays lighter, which is what every
# light theme does rather than an oversight: more ink is what reads as emphasis
# on paper, but bright black is the dimmed-comment gray everywhere.
#
# Purple stands in for magenta, and teal takes the cyan slot — steel cyan sits
# too close to the blue it would keep landing beside, so it stays a diagram
# color.
#
# This replaced a version that patched slots one at a time: red and cyan
# rendered identically in normal and bright, and bright white was the same ink
# as black.

